---
import AppShell from '../../layouts/AppShell.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { ORGANIZATION_REF, SOCIAL_IMAGE_URL, WEBSITE_REF } from '../../lib/seo';

export const prerender = true;

const title = 'Hire Neil Busque | AI Engineer and Product Builder';
const description = 'Hire Neil Busque to build an AI agent, automation, web app, or search-ready website. Based in New Jersey and available for focused projects.';
const canonical = 'https://busqueneil.com/hire';

const service = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  '@id': `${canonical}#service`,
  name: 'Neil Busque | AI Engineering and Automation',
  url: canonical,
  image: SOCIAL_IMAGE_URL,
  provider: ORGANIZATION_REF,
  brand: ORGANIZATION_REF,
  isPartOf: WEBSITE_REF,
  mainEntityOfPage: { '@id': `${canonical}#webpage` },
  areaServed: ['New Jersey', 'New York', 'United States', 'Remote'],
  serviceType: [
    'AI agent development',
    'AI automation',
    'Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)',
    'SEO',
    'Web app development',
    'Marketing automation',
  ],
  description,
};
---
<AppShell title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} active="hire">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <Breadcrumb items={[
      { name: 'Home', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/' },
      { name: 'Hire', url: canonical },
    ]} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(service)} />
  </Fragment>

  <span class="eyebrow">Hire</span>
  <h1 class="sec">Let's build the <span class="mark-hl">useful version.</span></h1>
  <p class="hero-sub">I am Neil Busque, an AI engineer and product builder in New Jersey. I build agents, automations, web apps, and websites for small teams. You work with me directly, and you can see the work before you hire me.</p>

  <!-- The five real steps. Each carries an on-brand mark drawn on the same 12-unit grid as
       the site's hairline module, so the icons read as part of the Blueprint system rather
       than as stock glyphs dropped in. -->
  <section class="process">
    <span class="eyebrow">How it goes</span>
    <h2 class="sec">Call to <span class="mark-hl">live.</span></h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect class="cell" x="6" y="10" width="36" height="24" rx="3" />
            <path d="M14 20h14M14 26h8" />
            <path d="M18 34l-4 6 10-6" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="step-n">01</span>
        <b>We talk through the problem</b>
        <span>You tell me what is happening now and what a good outcome looks like. If I am not the right fit, I say so here.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M8 12h32M8 24h32M8 36h20" />
            <rect class="cell" x="8" y="18" width="12" height="12" />
            <path d="M34 32l4 4 6-8" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="step-n">02</span>
        <b>I scope the project</b>
        <span>I write down what gets built, what does not, and the decisions we still need to make.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect class="cell" x="10" y="8" width="28" height="32" rx="3" />
            <path d="M17 18h14M17 25h14" />
            <path d="M17 32h7" />
            <circle cx="33" cy="33" r="5" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="step-n">03</span>
        <b>We agree on it</b>
        <span>We settle the scope, timeline, and price before the work starts.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect class="cell" x="6" y="12" width="36" height="26" rx="3" />
            <path d="M6 19h36" />
            <path d="M18 27l-4 4 4 4M30 27l4 4-4 4" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="step-n">04</span>
        <b>I build, you review</b>
        <span>You see the build as it takes shape and can change direction while changes are still cheap.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M8 34l8-9 7 6 8-12 9 7" />
            <rect class="cell" x="30" y="14" width="10" height="10" />
            <path d="M8 40h32" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="step-n">05</span>
        <b>Then we watch it work</b>
        <span>Once it is live, we fix the parts real use exposes. Keep me on for that or take it in-house.</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <article class="article-page">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What I build for you</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI agents and LLM apps.</strong> Agents that answer leads, update your CRM, draft content, or run research, with approval steps where people still need control.</li>
        <li><strong>Workflow automation.</strong> The manual, repetitive work in your business turned into pipelines that run themselves, in n8n, Zapier, and GoHighLevel.</li>
        <li><strong>Search and AI visibility.</strong> Helpful pages, technical SEO, and a site structure that search engines and AI-powered search can understand. See <a href="/guides/geo-generative-engine-optimization-guide">my AI search guide</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Custom web apps and PWAs.</strong> Internal tools, portals, dashboards, customer-facing apps. Shipped in days, not quarters. Here is <a href="/guides/ship-web-app-in-days-with-ai">how</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>UI and UX design.</strong> The interface, not just the wiring underneath it. Layout, hierarchy, type, and the flow a person actually takes through the screen, plus an honest read on why a page you already have is not converting.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>See the work before we talk</h2>
      <p>In 2026 I shipped more than 40 web apps, AI agents, and automations, including a CRM, a client portal, a link shortener, a cold-email app, and the CMS behind this site. Browse <a href="/work">the work</a> and read <a href="/resources">the guides</a>. You should not have to take my process on faith.</p>

      <h2>Two ways to work with me</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Join your team.</strong> Full-time work as an AI, automation, or growth engineer. I bring an engineering mindset and years of hands-on marketing experience. <a href="/resume.pdf">Read my resume</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Build one focused project.</strong> One agent, automation, app, or search-content overhaul. The scope is clear before I start.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why me</h2>
      <p>I came to AI through web development, design, automation, SEO, and paid media. That mix helps me spot when the right answer is an agent, when it is a plain workflow, and when the product problem has nothing to do with AI at all.</p>
      <p>Design is not an afterthought either. I <a href="/posts/why-i-build-apps">started out as a graphic designer</a> before I built software, so I work on the UI and UX myself and I can tell you why a page feels cheap, where a layout is losing people, and what to change: hierarchy, spacing, type, contrast, and the small bits of motion that make an interface feel finished. Plenty of people can build exactly what you asked for. Fewer can look at the result and say what is wrong with it.</p>
      <p>If the question behind your search is why hire anyone when AI can build it, I wrote the honest answer with receipts: <a href="/guides/why-hire-a-person-when-ai-can-build-it">six defects AI shipped for me that passed every check</a>, what each one cost, and the review layer that caught them.</p>

      <h2>Hire me</h2>
      <p>Tell me what is not working and what you want to be different. I will tell you honestly whether I am the right person for it.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:busqueneil@gmail.com">busqueneil@gmail.com</a></li>
        <li>LinkedIn: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/neilbusque" rel="me">linkedin.com/in/neilbusque</a></li>
        <li>Resume: <a href="/resume.pdf">busqueneil.com/resume.pdf</a></li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Project services</h2>
      <p>If you already know the shape of the work, start from the service instead:
        <a href="/services/ai-automation-services">AI automation services</a>,
        <a href="/services/ai-agent-development">AI agent development</a>, or
        <a href="/services/ai-automation-consultant">AI automation consulting</a>.</p>

      <h2>By location</h2>
      <p>Hiring for a specific area? <a href="/hire/ai-engineer-nj">AI engineer in New Jersey</a>, <a href="/hire/ai-engineer-nyc">AI engineer in NYC</a>, or <a href="/hire/ai-engineer-remote">remote AI engineer</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="hire-cta v8-card">
    <span class="eyebrow">The guarantee</span>
    <p class="guarantee">I keep working until you are proud of it. If I am not the right fit, I will tell you on the first call, and it costs you nothing.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn-sun" href="https://book.busqueneil.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a call</a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="https://wa.me/19083164140?text=Hi%20Neil%2C%20I%20have%20a%20project%20in%20mind" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Or message me on WhatsApp</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</AppShell>
